      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "helps them manage Bitcoin responsibly.\n\n Another important element of
    managing Bitcoin is understanding how to store assets for both short-term and
    long-term needs. Short-term holdings might remain in a hot wallet for convenience,
    while long-term investments are better stored in secure cold storage. This separation
    reduces risk in case a frequently used wallet becomes compromised. Users should
    periodically review their storage strategy to ensure it still fits their goals.
    Proper allocation between hot and cold wallets improves both safety and flexibility.\n\n
    Risk management plays a major role in successful Bitcoin ownership. Setting clear
    investment limits prevents emotional decisions during market volatility. Many
    users adopt strategies like dollar-cost averaging or setting stop-loss levels
    to protect their holdings. It\u2019s also wise to diversify and avoid putting
    all funds into one asset, even if Bitcoin is the primary "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
